  summary: `# 🦠 Zoonoses #6 — Helminthic Zoonoses

## 🎯 Three classes of helminths
- **Nematodes (roundworms)** — *Toxocara*, *Trichinella*, *Ancylostoma*
- **Cestodes (tapeworms)** — *Taenia*, *Echinococcus*, *Hymenolepis*
- **Trematodes (flukes)** — *Opisthorchis*, *Schistosoma*, *Fasciola*

## 🪱 Major helminthic zoonoses

| Disease | Pathogen | Definitive | Transmission |
|---|---|---|---|
| Toxocariasis (VLM/OLM) | *Toxocara canis*, *T. cati* | Dog/cat | Egg fecal-oral |
| Trichinellosis | *Trichinella spiralis* | Pig (carnivore) | Undercooked pork/wild meat |
| Cysticercosis | *Taenia solium* | Human | Egg fecal-oral (humans → cysts) |
| Echinococcosis | *Echinococcus granulosus* | Dog | Egg fecal-oral (sheep cycle) |
| Opisthorchiasis | *Opisthorchis viverrini* | Human | Raw/undercooked fish |
| Hookworm CLM | *Ancylostoma braziliense* | Dog/cat | Skin penetration (sand) |
| Anisakiasis | *Anisakis* spp. | Marine mammals | Raw fish (sushi) |

## 🐶 Toxocariasis (VLM/OLM)
- Adult worms in dog (*T. canis*) / cat (*T. cati*) intestine
- Eggs in feces → embryonate in soil
- Human ingest egg → larva migrate (visceral or ocular)
- Children (geophagia) at risk
- Dx: serology (ELISA), eosinophilia
- Tx: albendazole or mebendazole

## 🐷 Trichinellosis
- *T. spiralis* in skeletal muscle of pig/wild boar/horse
- Undercooked meat → larva → adult in human gut → larva re-migrate to muscle
- Clinical: GI (early), myalgia + periorbital edema (late)
- Dx: serology, muscle biopsy
- Tx: albendazole + steroids
- Prevention: cook pork ≥71°C, freeze -25°C 10 days

## 🪱 Taeniasis + Cysticercosis (T. solium)

| Form | Transmission | Result |
|---|---|---|
| Taeniasis | Eat pork with cysticercus | Adult tapeworm in gut (mild) |
| Cysticercosis | Eat T. solium egg (fecal-oral) | Cysticerci in muscle/CNS (severe!) |

- **Neurocysticercosis** = #1 cause of acquired epilepsy worldwide
- Endemic: developing countries with free-range pigs
- Tx: praziquantel (gut) or albendazole + steroids (CNS)

## 🐕 Echinococcosis (CE)
- Dog = definitive (eggs in feces)
- Sheep = intermediate (hydatid cysts in liver/lung)
- Human = accidental intermediate (egg ingestion)
- Hydatid cysts grow slowly in liver/lung/brain
- Endemic: pastoral regions (Tibet, Andes, ME)
- Dx: imaging + serology
- Tx: surgery + albendazole

## 🐟 Opisthorchiasis (Thailand!)
- *O. viverrini* — Mekong region (NE TH, Laos, Cambodia)
- Snail → cyprinid fish → human (raw/fermented fish — ปลาส้ม, ก้อย, ปลาดิบ)
- Adult fluke in bile duct → cholangitis → cholangiocarcinoma (CCA)
- **TH NE has world's highest CCA incidence**
- Tx: praziquantel
- Prevention: cook fish, NO raw freshwater fish

## 🦟 CLM (Cutaneous Larva Migrans)
- *Ancylostoma braziliense* dog/cat hookworm
- Larva in beach sand → skin penetration → migration tunnels
- "Creeping eruption" — pruritic serpiginous track
- Self-limiting, ivermectin/albendazole

## 🐟 Anisakiasis
- Marine mammal hookworm-like
- Raw fish (sushi, ceviche) → larva in human gut
- Eosinophilic gastritis
- Endoscopic removal

## 📝 EXAM RECAP
1. ⭐ Opisthorchis = NE Thailand → CCA (cholangiocarcinoma)
2. ⭐ T. solium cysticercosis → neurocysticercosis (epilepsy)
3. ⭐ Echinococcus: dog-sheep cycle, hydatid cysts
4. ⭐ Toxocara: VLM/OLM in children (geophagia)
5. ⭐ Trichinella: pork freezing -25°C 10d kills`,
